# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in.
#
# The two variables are no longer the same value, and the difference is
# load-bearing — see the "Base URL of our own NestJS API" comment in lib/api.ts.

# ── Server-only. Always ABSOLUTE. ────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Used by Server Components (`lib/api.ts`) and, in `next.config.js`, as the
# destination `/moviex/api/*` is proxied to. A relative path cannot work here:
# `fetch("/moviex/api/…")` from Node has no origin to resolve against.
#
# Server-to-server calls are not subject to browser cookie or CORS rules, so
# this stays pointed straight at the API — no reason to add a Vercel hop.
API_URL=https://moviex-skr4.onrender.com

# ── Client-side. Inlined into the browser bundle at BUILD time. ──────────────
#
# In production this is the RELATIVE proxy path, not a host:
#
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=/moviex/api
#
# The browser then only ever talks to the site's own origin
# (`habiboff.cc/moviex/api/*`), Vercel's `rewrites()` forwards to Render, and
# the session cookie comes back scoped to `habiboff.cc` — same-site, so plain
# `SameSite=Lax` works and mobile Safari/WebKit stops dropping it.
#
# Next inlines `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` at build time: change it and restart the dev
# server (or rebuild), or the old value stays compiled into the client bundle.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=/moviex/api

# Two alternatives, both fine locally:
#
#   1. Run Nest locally and talk to it directly. The dev API issues a
#      non-Secure `SameSite=Lax` cookie and localhost:3001 → localhost:3000 is
#      same-site, so this always works:
#        API_URL=http://localhost:3000
#        NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:3000
#
#   2. Testing from a phone on the LAN with a local API: both must be the dev
#      machine's LAN IP on the API's port (3000), and the frontend has to be
#      opened at http://<LAN-IP>:3001 too — a phone cannot resolve `localhost`
#      to your machine, and a mismatch makes the app look permanently signed
#      out. e.g. http://192.168.1.10:3000
#
# Note the app itself now lives under a base path: http://localhost:3001/moviex
